treaty calling for border demarcation , which the two presidents <ei22 signed> last May . In effect , the treaty amounts to Russian recognition of Ukraine 's sovereignty and borders , and the Ukrainian parliament has already <ei24 ratified> it . However , Russia has <ei25 stalled> <ei26 ratification> , <ei27 trying> to <ei28 tie> it to an <ei29 agreement> that would <ei30 permit> the Russian navy to <ei31 use> a naval base on Ukraine 's Crimean peninsula for at least 20 more years . In their joint statement <ei33 issued> after the <ei34 talks> , Yeltsin and Kuchma <ei35 called> for the fastest possible <ei36 ratification> of the treaty , <ei37 saying> it would <ei38 create> a \" strong legal foundation \" for bilateral ties and <ei39 help> stability in Europe . Kuchma <ei40 assured> Yeltsin that Ukraine would not <ei41 join> NATO , Yeltsin 's spokesman Sergei Yastrzhembsky <ei42 said> , <ei43 according> to the Interfax news agency . The Russian leadership has staunchly <ei44 opposed> the western alliance 's <ei45 expansion> into Eastern Europe . In their joint statement , <ei46 released> by the Kremlin , the two leaders also <ei47 pledged> to <ei48 consult> each other regularly on their approaches to relations with NATO and , in particular , their action within the framework of NATO 's Partnership for Peace program . Last year , Russian officials <ei50 assailed> Ukraine for <ei51 holding> joint naval <ei52 exercises> with NATO in the Black Sea _ an area Moscow considers its own turf . Kuchma has <ei53 said> repeatedly that Ukraine would <ei54 remain> neutral for the foreseeable future . Yeltsin and Kuchma also <ei55 called> for <ei56 developing> the stagnant relations between the members of the Commonwealth of Independent States , a loose coalition of former Soviet republics . In the past , Russia has often <ei58 claimed> that Ukraine was <ei59 undermining> efforts at closer cooperation within the CIS . A major goal of Kuchma 's four-day state <ei61 visit> was the <ei62 signing> of a 10-year economic program <ei64 aimed> at <ei65 doubling> the two nations ' trade turnover , which <ei66 fell> to dlrs 14 billion last year , down dlrs 2.5 billion from 1996 . The two presidents on Friday <ei70 signed> the plan , which <ei71 calls> for <ei72 cooperation> in the metallurgy , fuel , energy , aircraft building , missile , space and chemical industries . A major project is joint <ei73 manufacturing> of An-70 cargo planes , the Kremlin statement <ei74 said> . The program also <ei75 calls> for <ei76 coordination> of economic reforms and joint <ei77 improvement> of social programs in the two countries , where many people have become <ei78 impoverished> during the chaotic post-Soviet <ei79 transition> to capitalism . Kuchma also <ei80 planned> to <ei81 visit> Russian gas giant Gazprom , most likely to <ei82 discuss> Ukraine 's dlrs 1.2 billion debt to the company . ( pvs / vi / ji )", "gold": [["ei29", "causes", "ei31"], ["ei31", "causedby", "ei29"]], "lang": "eng", "mentions": ["ei1", "ei3", "ei4", "ei5", "ei7", "ei8", "ei9", "ei10", "ei11", "ei12", "ei13", "ei14", "ei15", "ei16", "ei17", "ei18", "ei19", "ei20", "ei21", "ei22", "ei24", "ei25", "ei26", "ei27", "ei28", "ei29", "ei30", "ei31", "ei33", "ei34", "ei35", "ei36", "ei37", "ei38", "ei39", "ei40", "ei41", "ei42", "ei43", "ei44", "ei45", "ei46", "ei47", "ei48", "ei50", "ei51", "ei52", "ei53", "ei54", "ei55", "ei56", "ei58", "ei59", "ei61", "ei62", "ei64", "ei65", "ei66", "ei70", "ei71", "ei72", "ei73", "ei74", "ei75", "ei76", "ei77", "ei78", "ei79", "ei80", "ei81", "ei82"], "surfaces": {"ei1": "signed", "ei3": "claimed", "ei4": "resolved", "ei5": "ruled", "ei7": "breakup", "ei8": "bedeviled", "ei9": "disputes", "ei10": "covered", "ei11": "discussed", "ei12": "tackling", "ei13": "quoted", "ei14": "saying", "ei15": "say", "ei16": "solved", "ei17": "disputes", "ei18": "resolved", "ei19": "require", "ei20": "compromise", "ei21": "dispute", "ei22": "signed", "ei24": "ratified", "ei25": "s